{:activity/_scope [{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101668} :activity/id #uuid "c8c3c4ee-2322-5eb7-80b7-81716b081931" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050825} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101668 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101956 :tutorial/content "To multiply a matrix by a column vector, we multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product.\n\nFor example, suppose we would like to multiply \n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nFirst, we write the multiplication as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe result of the multiplication is another column vector $\\mathbf{y}$ with the same dimensions as $\\mathbf{x}$.\nNow, we calculate the entries of the product (shown as $\\ast$'s in the equation above).\n\nTo find $y_1,$ the $1$st component of $\\mathbf{y}$, we calculate the dot product of the $1$st row of $A$ and the vector $\\mathbf{x}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find $y_2,$ the $2$nd component of $\\mathbf{y},$ we calculate the dot product of the $2$nd row of $A$ and the vector $\\mathbf{x}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "1f07e56d-40c7-5691-b5d8-8f35492a53fc" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2987 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "bbb9f137-421c-5536-8a14-dcbb66d8d180" :step/math-academy-id 16171 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101669}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101669 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100866 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100688 :question/id #uuid "f31d614e-a00c-5502-8b23-e9214bc2ae5c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4397" :question/problem "Find $A\\mathbf{x}$ if \n![](images/cd/cd3816d9938d4bd65d0eaa5abcb3db329aed3827219a8cea0186ced2d5759880.png)\nand\n![](images/b9/b9c909115c604eb1a96463bdd31a71e77caa0a11d0098a8144afd798b50ae236.png)" :question/worked-solution "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product. Multiplying the first row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 5 \\\\ ∗\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}17 \\\\ ∗\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}17 \\\\ 7\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot 5\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}17 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n![](images/6d/6d470181fba760868835a72c5d5cfec3c90f9bf7bf7a9d86860dc8d981517652.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff414112-3be2-5b9c-9ded-5025ea05c2b4" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048896} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048954}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550169 :question-generator/id #uuid "9a0d1aec-6f6f-5be5-86e3-efa16be008e1" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186100866.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101136 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ce47e15-8a71-5a0e-877b-8161ee17ff71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388418} {:answer/id #uuid "84d4840e-ffea-5fc0-bd15-47e2b8b3ee8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388419} {:answer/id #uuid "a052459a-e452-5bfb-9115-9b9d15dcfb91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388420} {:answer/id #uuid "b4829af7-c55a-5072-9da4-2384966bfee9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\be