/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6a+2c \\\\ b+2d\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564822} {:answer/id #uuid "c868914e-80f6-580f-a58e-37b2ba156acf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3a+2c \\\\ 2b+2d\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564830} {:answer/id #uuid "d0fa1408-3d85-5508-9714-e2aa37808ca6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3a+2c \\\\ b+d\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564833}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564819} :answer-field/id #uuid "5153c977-ef10-5450-bc37-08dfa786973d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564808}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f194822e-641e-5dbc-922a-c09d1ee8c7ac" :question/problem "Find $Ax$ if\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}3a & c \\\\ b & d\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$x = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$." :question/worked-solution "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =\\begin{bmatrix}3a & c \\\\ b & d\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & =\\begin{bmatrix}3a\\cdot 1+c\\cdot 2 \\\\ b\\cdot 1+d\\cdot 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & =\\begin{bmatrix}3a+2c \\\\ b+2d\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Matrix With Variable Entries by a Column Vector"} :step/id #uuid "a8c7ed6f-0bf9-5ea9-afaa-10a1cd83164a" :step/math-academy-id 16174 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101672}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101672 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101957 :tutorial/content "An alternative, yet equivalent, procedure for multiplying a matrix by a column vector involves adding scaled columns of the matrix $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =\\begin{bmatrix}a & c \\\\ b & d\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ d\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3a \\\\ 3b\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2c \\\\ 2d\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3a+2c \\\\ 3b+2d\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote \n$\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$\\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ d\\end{bmatrix}$ \nthen we can also write the multiplication as follows:\n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{x}={\\color{blue}3}\\mathbf{u}_1 + {\\color{blue}2} \\mathbf{u}_2\n$$\n\nThe expression above is a **linear combination** of the vectors $\\mathbf{u}_1$ and $\\mathbf{u}_2,$ where the corresponding coefficients are given by the entries of the vector $\\mathbf{x}.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "ba7586ab-f421-5676-ab23-cfc9484ae9f1" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2988 :tutorial/title "Alternative Rule"} :step/id #uuid "0b6496a4-1d4a-5439-8b74-e7c9214981e4" :step/math-academy-id 16175}] :activity/title "Multiplying a Matrix by a Column Vector" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186101054}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186050825 :topic/difficulty 0.48023065847230173 :topic/id #uuid "69b57f07-ad86-5963-8f81-f63cb01f239f" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100866 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100688 :question/id #uuid "f31d614e-a00c-5502-8b23-e9214bc2ae5c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4397" :question/problem "Find $A\\mathbf{x}$ if \n![](images/cd/cd3816d9938d4bd65d0eaa5abcb3db329aed3827219a8cea0186ced2d5759880.png)\nand\n![](images/b9/b9c909115c604eb1a96463bdd31a71e77caa0a11d0098a8144afd798b50ae236.png)" :question/worked-solution "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product. Multiplying the first row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 5 \\\\ ∗\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}17 \\\\ ∗\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}17 \\\\ 7\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot 5\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}17 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n![](images/6d/6d470181fba760868835a72c5d5cfec3c90f9bf7bf7a9d86860dc8d981517652.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff414112-3be2-5b9c-9ded-5025ea05c2b4" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048896} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048954}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550169 :question-generator/id #uuid "9a0d1aec-6f6f-5be5-86e3-efa16be008e1" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186100866.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101136 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ce47e15-8a71-5a0e-877b-8161ee17ff71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388418} {:answer/id #uuid "84d4840e-ffea-5fc0-bd15-47e2b8b3ee8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388419} {:answer/id #uuid "a052459a-e452-5bfb-9115-9b9d15dcfb91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388420} {:answer/id #uuid "b4829af7-c55a-5072-9da4-2384966bfee9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388421} {:answer/id #uuid "f605914a-ff93-5823-885b-2509f3adee21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388422}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388422} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef949d1a-3425-5215-bdb0-047bedfe1e0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c